# The actual relative invariant unit-phase homotopy

The normalized real segment between a continuous unit phase and a continuous
half-unit-close approximation is a native circle-valued homotopy. The whole
segment stays nonzero, and the same explicit homotopy preserves agreement on
any prescribed set and invariance under any given family of self-maps.

There are no smoothness or manifold assumptions on the continuous source.
